---
title: Conditions
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

## If

Each `If` command runs the commands up to its matching `Else` or `EndIf` only when its condition is true. `Else` is optional:

```c
IfEq(GF_KMR02_WarpPipe, false)
    Call(SpeakToPlayer, NPC_PARTNER, ANIM_Goompa_Talk, ANIM_Goompa_Idle, 0, MSG_CH0_001C)
Else
    Wait(10)
EndIf
```

| Command | Runs when |
| --- | --- |
| `IfEq(A, B)` | `A == B` |
| `IfNe(A, B)` | `A != B` |
| `IfLt(A, B)` | `A < B` |
| `IfGt(A, B)` | `A > B` |
| `IfLe(A, B)` | `A <= B` |
| `IfGe(A, B)` | `A >= B` |
| `IfRange(A, MIN, MAX)` | `MIN <= A <= MAX` |
| `IfNotRange(A, MIN, MAX)` | `A < MIN` or `A > MAX` |
| `IfTrue(A)` | `A != 0` |
| `IfFalse(A)` | `A == 0` |
| `IfFlag(A, BITS)` | Any of `BITS` are set in `A` |
| `IfNotFlag(A, BITS)` | None of `BITS` are set in `A` |
| `IfEval(FUNC, ARGS...)` | The C function returns something other than zero. See [Call C functions](/papermario-dx/evt-scripts/call-c). |
| `IfNotEval(FUNC, ARGS...)` | The C function returns zero. |
| `IfEvalF(FUNC, ARGS...)` | As `IfEval`, for a function that takes decimal numbers. |
| `IfNotEvalF(FUNC, ARGS...)` | As `IfNotEval`, for a function that takes decimal numbers. |
| `Else` | Starts the commands that run when the condition is false. |
| `EndIf` | Ends the `If`. |

## Switch

To choose between several values, use a `Switch`. `Switch(A)` compares `A` against each case in turn and runs the first case that matches:

```c
Call(GetEntryID, LVar0)
Switch(LVar0)
    CaseEq(kmr_02_ENTRY_0)
        Exec(EVS_ArriveFromVillage)
    CaseEq(kmr_02_ENTRY_1)
        Exec(EVS_ArriveFromForest)
    CaseDefault
        Exec(EVS_ArriveSomewhereElse)
EndSwitch
```

Unlike in C, a case doesn't continue into the next one. Switches can be nested up to 8 deep.

| Command | Matches when |
| --- | --- |
| `CaseEq(B)` | `A == B` |
| `CaseNe(B)` | `A != B` |
| `CaseLt(B)` | `A < B` |
| `CaseGt(B)` | `A > B` |
| `CaseLe(B)` | `A <= B` |
| `CaseGe(B)` | `A >= B` |
| `CaseRange(MIN, MAX)` | `MIN <= A <= MAX` |
| `CaseFlag(BITS)` | Any of `BITS` are set in `A` |
| `CaseDefault` | Always. Put it last. |
| `CaseOrEq(B)` | `A == B`. Consecutive `CaseOrEq` cases share the commands that follow them, up to `EndCaseGroup`. |
| `CaseAndEq(B)` | `A == B`, like `CaseOrEq`, but stops the group when it doesn't match. |
| `EndCaseGroup` | Ends a group of `CaseOrEq` or `CaseAndEq` cases. |
| `BreakSwitch` | Leaves the switch. |
| `EndSwitch` | Ends the switch. |
| `SwitchConst(A)` | Like `Switch`, but uses `A` as written, without reading it as a variable. |
